From: ios14-lithium
Subject: [build] allow a kernel without a matching kext profiling provider

XNU7195 declares the old six-range compiler-rt API. Current compiler-rt
uses another API and raw format; linking it by name would be an ABI error.
The bring-up build explicitly sets XNU_KEXT_PGO=0 and reports ENOTSUP for
profiling queries. The normal source path remains the default otherwise.
No dummy profiling output or success return is introduced.

diff --git a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
--- a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
@@ -10158,6 +10158,9 @@
     char *pBuffer,
     uint64_t bufferSize)
 {
+#if defined(XNU_KEXT_PGO) && !XNU_KEXT_PGO
+	return ENOTSUP;
+#else
 	int err = 0;
 
 	kernel_section_t *sect_prf_data = NULL;
@@ -10241,6 +10244,7 @@
 
 out:
 	return err;
+#endif
 }
 
 
